Title: Shell script quality and validation

Scope:
- Applies to all shell scripts (`.sh` files) in the codebase.
- Includes scripts in `scripts/`, `package/scripts/`, and any other directories.

Requirements:
- **Shellcheck validation**: Any modification to a shell script MUST be validated using `shellcheck`.
- **MANDATORY**: When editing or creating a shell script, the AI assistant MUST run `shellcheck <path to script>` to validate the script.
- All shellcheck errors and warnings must be addressed before the changes are considered complete.
- Shellcheck should be run automatically as part of the editing workflow for shell scripts.

Tooling:
- `shellcheck` must be installed and available in the PATH.
- If `shellcheck` is not installed, install it using your system's package manager:
  - macOS: `brew install shellcheck`
  - Linux: `apt-get install shellcheck` or `yum install shellcheck`
  - Or download from: https://github.com/koalaman/shellcheck

Acceptance checklist for shell script changes:
- [ ] `shellcheck <path to script>` passes without errors.
- [ ] All shellcheck warnings have been addressed or explicitly ignored with appropriate comments.
- [ ] Script follows shell scripting best practices (proper quoting, error handling, etc.).
